# SR: the four-card platform replay of the NEW production image: the node agent's serving sequence on all four boards (resolved at run time: none named) in a copy of its container
# running the THIN LAYER image (@THIN_LAYER_IMAGE@: the platform image built on tp4-serve-9 and pre-pulled into the rig daemon, given by the manifest-list digest: the daemon uses
# the containerd image store and a config digest does not resolve). C2_REPLAY_PROFILE is the profile the copy must BOOT BY THE IMAGE DEFAULT: the agent forwards no QWEN_C2_PROFILE,
# so the replay sets none either, and the profile it boots is the one baked into the image's ENV. Each boot's (load, reload, restart) vLLM subprocess log, read from the container
# (never docker logs), must show '[QWEN-C2] profile c2-packed-tp4-best-ship: vLLM argv', the P150x4 mesh line, admission passed with no UNQUALIFIED, parser M armed, 'extent replay
# engaged' and the prefill warm checks; the platform's served name (the :tt alias) must be advertised before and after the restart. Pass: 'PLATFORM_REPLAY passed=True'.
# The replay turns the session cap OFF in its own environment, so it cannot show the cap: B0's provenance read the baked pair, and the cap is read live after the placement.
# C2_REPLAY_BUDGET_SMOKE=1 also runs the image's thinking-budget smoke in the replay's container before it is removed, up to 90 minutes, and fails the job if it ran and failed.
# Duration (estimate): 45-60 min plus the smoke (up to 90), then H's reset. Stop rule: any FAIL stops the window: :latest does not move.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/next-4 four-seat SHIP window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/next-4 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a
# registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The window's jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from this branch by its author.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-serve-9 is the SHIPPING base B0 builds from the pushed tp4/next-4 commit with the candidate profile
# c2-packed-tp4-best-ship baked in as the image's serving default (ENV QWEN_C2_PROFILE) and the platform session cap baked as its seat count (4). Every job
# serves that one image, so the bytes that pass are the bytes that ship. Each job still names its profile explicitly, so none relies on the baked default.
# qwen_c2_profiles.json's own default stays c2-packed-tp4: only a build that names C2_BAKE_DEFAULT_PROFILE (B0's one key) bakes anything. A commit that
# changes a file the image carries needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every template.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset replay
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-serve-9
C2_PLATFORM_IMAGE=@THIN_LAYER_IMAGE@
C2_REPLAY_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-best-ship
C2_REPLAY_BUDGET_SMOKE=1
